    "observations": [
      "Net gamma exposure is positive at the close: dealers are long gamma and hedge against the direction of price moves",
      "Spot closed above the zero-gamma level and almost on top of the call wall, so the market sits on the long-gamma side of the flip point with the nearest reference level directly overhead",
      "The put wall is well below spot; the reference range between the walls is wide on the downside and nearly exhausted on the upside",
      "The twenty-five delta put skew is inside GaleCore's calm zone and the wing premium over the at-the-money is modest",
      "The volatility index settled in the mid teens and the vol-of-vol index is subdued, consistent with an options market that is not pricing an imminent shock"
    ],
    "implications": [
      "With dealers long gamma, hedging flows should dampen moves and favour mean reversion, so realized volatility is expected to stay contained while the regime holds",
      "The call wall sitting on top of spot is where hedging resistance would first be expected; the flip point below is the level whose loss would change the character of hedging flows",
      "A calm skew alongside positive gamma is a coherent combination: the options market is not paying up for protection while hedging flows are counter-cyclical"
    ],
